! DF'S MASK-DEPENDENT HALF AT p.32'S CLASS 3 -- the refill does not
! happen and the whole operation is SUPPRESSED.  The companion to
! df_refill_alarm.strap and df_refill_index_alarm.strap, which run the
! mask-ZERO case for the same six sites and scoped this one out because
! the model had no suppression at those sites at all.
!
! THE CATEGORY, Reference Manual printed p.32 (PDF 35), read first-hand
! at 300 dpi.  "Address monitoring for Data Fetch includes: ... 3. The
! refill address used in index refill operations and the operations
! REFILL and REFILL ON COUNT ZERO."  That is its own numbered class,
! beside class 1's "effective address of all fetch-type operations with
! a direct address" -- so the mask rule three paragraphs earlier on the
! same page reaches it directly: "If the DF mask bit is one, the data
! fetch is suppressed and the operation terminated.  If the DF mask bit
! is zero, the operation proceeds normally."
!
! WHAT "THE OPERATION" MEANS, printed p.45 (PDF 48), indicator 20: "If
! the corresponding mask bit was one, the fetch did not take place, and
! THE ENTIRE OPERATION WAS SUPPRESSED.  If the mask bit was zero, the
! operation was completed normally."  Not merely the fetch.
!
! AND THE MANUAL WORKS THIS EXACT CASE, printed p.52 (PDF 55), read
! first-hand at 300 dpi.  It is better authority than either sentence
! above, because it is the only place that says what a suppressed
! count-branch-refill does about its BRANCH:
!
!   "Since an instruction is fully interpreted before it can be
!   suppressed, more than one alert of Class S can be caused by the
!   instruction.  For example, if a STORE INSTRUCTION COUNTER IF COUNT,
!   BRANCH AND REFILL is executed as the subject instruction of
!   EXECUTE, it is possible for (1) the condition for branching to be
!   met, (2) the effective SIC address to be invalid, (3) the effective
!   branch address and the refill address to be protected, and (4) the
!   count to reach zero. ...  When, however, in this example, the
!   condition for branching is not met, the entire subject instruction
!   is still suppressed but only indicator DF is actuated (the DF mask
!   bit is assumed to be one).  Indicator DF is actuated since THE TEST
!   FOR THE REFILLING IS INDEPENDENT OF THE TEST FOR A SUCCESSFUL
!   BRANCH."
!
! Block C1 below is that sentence turned into a check: a CBRZ whose
! count reaches zero would BOTH refill AND branch, and with the mask at
! one it must do neither.  (CBRZ and not CBR, and the choice is forced:
! p.41's count-branch family branches on count NOT zero unless the
! branch-on-zero bit is set, and the refill fires when the count DOES
! reach zero, so plain CBR can never branch and refill on the same
! execution.  CBRZ is the only spelling in which the two coincide,
! which is exactly the coincidence p.52 describes.)
!
! THE SIX SITES, AND THE FIVE THIS DELIBERATELY DOES NOT TOUCH.
! StretchExecute.bsv has eleven class-3 refill reads.  Six are covered
! here -- CBR/CBRZ in evalBranch, V+CR in dirIndexOp, V+ICR and V-ICR
! in immIndexOp, and R/RCZ on both of their paths (the index-register
! one and the external-memory one that takes two sequential reads).
! The other five are the refills PROGRESSIVE INDEXING issues from the
! VFL and connective formats, and they are a DIFFERENT MECHANISM, not a
! missing line.  Printed p.53 (PDF 56), read first-hand, gives them
! their own rule, and it is the third entry under EXECUTION TERMINATED
! rather than under EXECUTION SUPPRESSED: "An alert of Class S during
! progressive indexing suppresses only the indexing portion of the
! operation."  Terminate, not suppress; separate work.
!
! WHAT SUPPRESSION LEAVES BEHIND (printed p.52): "the suppression of an
! instruction must necessarily exclude the following operations: 1. The
! actuation of those indicators, associated with the instruction, of
! Class S, and indicators DF and IF when their mask bits are zero. ...
! 3. The stepping of the instruction counter."  Item 1 is why every
! block below still expects DF to have been actuated; item 3 is why
! control reaches the check after the suppressed instruction at all.
!
! EVERY CHECK OBSERVES THE DESTINATION'S VALUE, never the operation's
! own result indicators -- the probe shape df_fetch_suppress.strap
! copied from routine 1260 TEST 8C, and it is load-bearing here for the
! same reason: a model that "suppressed" by writing zero, or by writing
! the un-refilled arithmetic result, would pass an indicator check and
! fail this one.  Concretely, each index register is loaded from a
! control word whose VALUE is PREVAL and whose REFILL field names
! RFSRC, whose value is a different constant.  Every operation below is
! arranged to leave the value field alone (CBRZ with no increment, V+CR
! against a zero operand, V+ICR/V-ICR with a zero immediate), so
! afterwards the register holds
!
!     RFSRC's value   the refill happened
!     PREVAL          the whole operation was suppressed
!
! and KV against RFCOPY or PRECOPY tells those two apart.  On the
! external-memory path the destination is not a register at all but the
! storage word R rewrites, so that block reads the word back with LX
! first; it does not inherit the register probe.
!
! V+CR'S OPERAND SITS OUTSIDE THE AREA ON PURPOSE.  V+CR monitors two
! addresses -- the operand half-word (class 1, already suppressing
! before this change) and the refill source (class 3, the new one).
! ZEROW is below the lower boundary so the class-1 gate cannot fire and
! the block names one address.
!
! THE NOPS AFTER EACH MASK-ONE OPERATION ARE NOT PADDING, the same
! reason df_fetch_suppress.strap gives: DF is masked ON in block C, so
! the violation is reported by INTERRUPTING, and this model takes an
! interruption at a QUIESCENT boundary rather than at the instruction
! boundary p.48 names.  The marker is word 7, which is in p.31's 0-31
! carve-out and so can never itself signal.
!
! STANDARD: MANUAL-DERIVED, hand-written.  Routine 1260 TEST 8C is the
! deck oracle for DF's mask bit, but its offending fetch is an LV --
! p.32 class 1 -- and no listing this project has read exercises a
! protected REFILL address with the mask at one.  p.52's worked example
! is the nearest primary source and it is prose, not code.
!
! EXPECTED STDERR ON A GREEN RUN -- read it, per
! df_refill_index_alarm.strap's note.  OBSERVED: nothing.  All six
! sites are I-Box class (half-word index arithmetic, count-branch, and
! the REFILL misc format), so none reaches the side-effect-free E-box
! probe that makes df_fetch_suppress.strap print "executed at
! preparation (classification mismatch)".
!
! NINE INJECTIONS, EACH OBSERVED (not predicted), AND ONE THAT SURVIVED
! AND IS RECORDED AS A GAP.  Reproduce any row with
! `python3 line_addresses.py programs/df_refill_suppress.strap`.
!
!   CBRZ suppression removed         -> 004161.00  CBRZ, $X1, $  (C1)
!                                         -- it branched to itself
!   suppressed CBRZ still BRANCHES   -> 004161.00  CBRZ, $X1, $  (C1)
!     (the index write suppressed,          -- p.52's own claim, and the
!      the branch not)                         only check that reaches it
!   V+CR suppression removed         -> 004200.40  BZB, $XE, $   (C2)
!   V+ICR suppression removed        -> 004211.00  BZB, $XE, $   (C3)
!   V-ICR suppression removed        -> 004221.40  BZB, $XE, $   (C4)
!   R/RCZ index-register path,       -> 004232.00  BZB, $XE, $   (C5)
!     suppression removed                   -- C6 (RCZ) shares that code
!                                              site with C5 (R), so C5 is
!                                              always the address reported
!                                              and C6 never appears in this
!                                              table.  It is a second
!                                              witness on the same arm, not
!                                              a seventh site; nothing here
!                                              distinguishes R from RCZ
!   R/RCZ external-memory path,      -> 004254.00  BZB, $XE, $   (C7)
!     suppression removed                 -- the STORAGE word was rewritten
!   the MASK gate dropped from       -> 004114.40  B, $          (B1)
!     dfSuppresses (suppress                -- the mask-ZERO case, which is
!     whenever protViolates fires)             why block B exists at all;
!                                              a suppressed CBRZ cannot branch
!   dfSignal skipped when            -> 004165.40  BZB, 7.0, $   (C1)
!     suppressing (p.52 item 1)           -- no indicator, so no interruption,
!                                            so the routine never ran
!
! THE ONE THAT SURVIVED, and it is a real gap in this program rather
! than a fault in the model.  Injection: at the evalBranch site, make
! the suppression test read `... && (prefetchCount >= slot + 1)`, so it
! fires only on the SECOND pass -- i.e. after the refill read has
! already been issued and its word landed in prefetch[slot].  The
! operation is still suppressed, the index register is still untouched,
! the branch still does not happen, DF is still set.  OBSERVED: ALL
! TESTS PASSED.
!
! It cannot be caught from a STRAP program in this model, and the
! bound is stateable: a refill read has no architecturally visible
! effect -- it writes no storage, sets no indicator, and this model
! exposes no cycle or read count to the program -- so the only trace of
! the wasted read would be the prefetch SLOT it consumes, and the one
! consumer of evalBranch's slot accounting is SIC, which requests its
! own read only `if (o.taken ...)` and a suppressed CBRZ is never taken.
! The ordering in StretchExecute.bsv is therefore justified by printed
! p.45's "the fetch did not take place" and not by this test, and the
! call site says so.
!
! Instructions: BD, BE, LVI, SV, LX, SX, KV, CBRZ, V+CR, V+ICR, V-ICR,
! R, RCZ, BB, BB1, BBZ, BZB, B, NOP, BEW -- all implemented.

        SLC, (8)4100.0
START   BD,  $+.32                   ! disable: words 3 and 12 come next
        LVI, $X13, TBL
        SV,  $X13, $IA
        LVI, $X13, RFSRC
        SV,  $X13, $LB               ! lower boundary := RFSRC
        LVI, $X13, ABOVE
        SV,  $X13, $UB               ! upper boundary := ABOVE
        BBZ, 3.57, $+1.0             ! control bit := 0: signal INSIDE
!
! ---- A. DISABLED, MASK ONE: the refill proceeds anyway ------------
!   TEST 8C case 2's shape.  p.32: "When the interruption system is
!   disabled, address monitoring is ineffective... the DS, DF and IF
!   indicators cannot be turned on when the system is disabled."  So
!   the mask bit is irrelevant here, and this block is carried by the
!   pre-existing enable gate inside protViolates, which dfSuppresses
!   shares.  It adds no discrimination for the new code -- recorded
!   here rather than discovered as a surviving injection.
        BB1, 12.20, $+1.0            ! DF's mask bit := ONE
        LX,  $X5,  KC0               ! value PREVAL, count 0, refill RFSRC
        R,   $X5
        BB,  $DF,  $                 ! hang if DF lit while disabled
        KV,  $X5,  RFCOPY
        BZB, $XE,  $                 ! hang if the refill did NOT happen
!
! ---- B. ENABLED, MASK ZERO: DF sets, the refill LANDS -------------
!   The half df_refill_alarm.strap and df_refill_index_alarm.strap
!   already test.  Repeated here at all six sites because IT IS WHAT
!   MAKES THE MASK GATE DISCRIMINATING: without a mask-zero case beside
!   each mask-one case, dropping `maskedOn(st, ind_DF)` from
!   dfSuppresses changes nothing this program can see.
        BBZ, 12.20, $+1.0            ! DF's mask bit := ZERO
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0             ! start from DF off
        BE,  $+.32                   ! ENABLE
!
! ---- B1. CBRZ: it branches AND refills ---------------------------
        LX,   $X1, KC1               ! count 1 -> 0
        CBRZ, $X1, BT1               ! branches (count reached zero) and
                                     !   refills from RFSRC
        B,    $                      ! hang if it did NOT branch
BT1     BZB,  $DF, $                 ! hang if the refill address missed DF
        BB,   $IF, $                 ! hang if it lit the NEIGHBOUR: DF is
                                     !   20 and IF is 21, and without this
                                     !   the injection that swaps them is
                                     !   indistinguishable from removal
        BBZ,  $DF, $+1.0
        KV,   $X1, RFCOPY
        BZB,  $XE, $                 ! hang if the refill did not land
!
! ---- B2. V+CR ----------------------------------------------------
        LX,   $X2, KC1
        V+CR, $X2, ZEROW             ! operand OUTSIDE the area: adds zero,
                                     !   count 1 -> 0, refills from RFSRC
        BZB,  $DF, $
        BBZ,  $DF, $+1.0
        KV,   $X2, RFCOPY
        BZB,  $XE, $
!
! ---- B3. V+ICR ---------------------------------------------------
        LX,    $X3, KC1
        V+ICR, $X3, 0                ! reads NO operand: the refill source
                                     !   is the only address it uses
        BZB,   $DF, $
        BBZ,   $DF, $+1.0
        KV,    $X3, RFCOPY
        BZB,   $XE, $
!
! ---- B4. V-ICR ---------------------------------------------------
        LX,    $X4, KC1
        V-ICR, $X4, 0
        BZB,   $DF, $
        BBZ,   $DF, $+1.0
        KV,    $X4, RFCOPY
        BZB,   $XE, $
!
! ---- B5. R, refilling an INDEX REGISTER --------------------------
        LX,  $X5,  KC0
        R,   $X5
        BZB, $DF,  $
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
        KV,  $X5,  RFCOPY
        BZB, $XE,  $
!
! ---- B6. RCZ, the other operation p.32 class 3 names -------------
!   Same code site as R above (the arm gates on "R, or RCZ whose count
!   is zero"), so this is a second witness rather than a seventh site.
        LX,  $X6,  KC0               ! count 0, so RCZ acts
        RCZ, $X6
        BZB, $DF,  $
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
        KV,  $X6,  RFCOPY
        BZB, $XE,  $
!
! ---- B7. R whose operand word is in EXTERNAL MEMORY --------------
!   Two sequential reads: the index word at the effective address, then
!   the word its refill field names.  EXIDX is OUTSIDE the area, so
!   only the second read can signal, and the DESTINATION is EXIDX
!   itself -- R writes the refill word back there.
        LX,  $X7,  KC0
        SX,  $X7,  EXIDX             ! plant the index word outside the area
        R,   EXIDX
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, $DF,  $
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
        LX,  $X7,  EXIDX             ! read the DESTINATION back
        KV,  $X7,  RFCOPY
        BZB, $XE,  $                 ! hang if the refill did not land
!
! ---- C. ENABLED, MASK ONE: the whole operation is SUPPRESSED ------
!   The indicator still sets -- p.52 item 1 -- and then INTERRUPTS,
!   because the mask bit is one.  rl_interrupt turns the causing
!   indicator off on its way into the routine (p.48), so after each
!   block DF reads OFF and the witness is the routine's own marker,
!   word 7.
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0             ! clear DF before arming its mask
        BB1, 12.20, $+1.0            ! DF's mask bit := ONE
!
! ---- C1. CBRZ: NEITHER refill NOR branch -- p.52's worked case ----
        LX,   $X1, KC1               ! the PRELOAD, which must survive
        CBRZ, $X1, $                 ! SUPPRESSED.  The target is this
                                     !   instruction itself, so a branch
                                     !   that is not suppressed hangs HERE
                                     !   -- which is the half p.45 alone
                                     !   does not reach and p.52 does
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB,  7.0, $                 ! hang if DF's routine did not run
        BBZ,  7.0, $+1.0
        KV,   $X1, PRECOPY
        BZB,  $XE, $                 ! hang if the refill landed after all
!
! ---- C2. V+CR ----------------------------------------------------
        LX,   $X2, KC1
        V+CR, $X2, ZEROW             ! SUPPRESSED by the REFILL address;
                                     !   the operand at ZEROW is outside
                                     !   the area, so the class-1 gate one
                                     !   level out cannot be what fired
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB,  7.0, $
        BBZ,  7.0, $+1.0
        KV,   $X2, PRECOPY
        BZB,  $XE, $
!
! ---- C3. V+ICR ---------------------------------------------------
        LX,    $X3, KC1
        V+ICR, $X3, 0                ! SUPPRESSED
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB,   7.0, $
        BBZ,   7.0, $+1.0
        KV,    $X3, PRECOPY
        BZB,   $XE, $
!
! ---- C4. V-ICR ---------------------------------------------------
        LX,    $X4, KC1
        V-ICR, $X4, 0                ! SUPPRESSED
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB,   7.0, $
        BBZ,   7.0, $+1.0
        KV,    $X4, PRECOPY
        BZB,   $XE, $
!
! ---- C5. R, index-register path ----------------------------------
        LX,  $X5,  KC0
        R,   $X5                     ! SUPPRESSED
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, 7.0,  $
        BBZ, 7.0,  $+1.0
        KV,  $X5,  PRECOPY
        BZB, $XE,  $
!
! ---- C6. RCZ, index-register path --------------------------------
        LX,  $X6,  KC0
        RCZ, $X6                     ! SUPPRESSED
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, 7.0,  $
        BBZ, 7.0,  $+1.0
        KV,  $X6,  PRECOPY
        BZB, $XE,  $
!
! ---- C7. R, external-memory path ---------------------------------
!   The destination is the STORAGE WORD at EXIDX, not a register, so
!   the probe reads it back rather than comparing an index value that
!   the operation never touches.
        LX,  $X7,  KC0
        SX,  $X7,  EXIDX             ! re-plant it: B7 above overwrote it
        R,   EXIDX                   ! SUPPRESSED
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, 7.0,  $
        BBZ, 7.0,  $+1.0
        LX,  $X7,  EXIDX             ! read the DESTINATION back
        KV,  $X7,  PRECOPY
        BZB, $XE,  $                 ! hang if EXIDX was rewritten
        B,   PASS
PASS    BEW, $
!
! ---- constants, all OUTSIDE the monitored area -------------------
        SLC, (8)4260.0
KC1     XW, (8)252525.00, 1, RFSRC   ! value PREVAL, count 1: the refill fires
KC0     XW, (8)252525.00, 0, RFSRC   ! value PREVAL, count 0: for R and RCZ
PRECOPY XW, (8)252525.00, 0, 0       ! the value a SUPPRESSED operation leaves
RFCOPY  XW, (8)123456.76, 0, 0       ! the value a refill that LANDED leaves
ZEROW   DD(BU,64,8), 0               ! V+CR's operand half-word: adds zero
EXIDX   NOP                          ! scratch: an index word is planted here
        NOP
!
! ---- the monitored area ------------------------------------------
!   The area is the HALF-OPEN interval [RFSRC, ABOVE) (p.31), so RFSRC
!   is protected and ABOVE is the first word outside it.
        SLC, (8)4300.0
RFSRC   XW, (8)123456.76, (8)543210, (8)123456   ! == the lower boundary
ABOVE   DD(BU,64,8), 0               ! == the upper boundary, first word out
!
! ---- the interruption table --------------------------------------
!   Entry N is at TBL + N words (p.48).  DF is indicator 20, so entry
!   20 is TBL + 0o24.  The DS entry is kept for the same reason
!   df_refill_alarm.strap keeps it: DS is permanently masked on, and a
!   stray store would otherwise run off into unloaded storage.
        SLC, (8)4500.0
TBL     DD, 0
        SLC, (8)4523.0
DSRTN   BB1, 6.0, $+1.0              ! entry 19 = DS
        SLC, (8)4524.0
DFRTN   BB1, 7.0, $+1.0              ! entry 20 = DF (0o4500 + 0o24)
        END, START
